Yes, you do need to make a mistake in planning or execution if you get
battered to death by air elementals on the planes from 500 hp.  Here are
some of the possibilities:

- you did not have a low enough AC
- you did not have enough /oTeleport
- you did not have enough !oFH, or use them at the right time
- you did not have enough /oDeath or other quick-kill methods
- you did not use conflict effectively
- you did not use other monsters as effective barriers
- you did not camp in vortices enough

Really, you have to make several of these mistakes for air elementals on
the astral plane to actually succeed at taking off 500 hp.  It should take
them several dozen turns to take off that many hp -- certainly long enough
to get out and quaff a !oFH.  And if they can't get to you, they can't
damage you.  And if they die to your /oDeath they'll only get one (or
zero) hits in.

Just about any death beyond the castle is due to a mistake in planning or
execution.  Death to air elementals is common, but not unavoidable -- if
you plan appropriately, you will not die to them.  Between my wife's 4
ascensions and my 3, air elementals on the plane of air were only truly a
threat the first time, because she didn't know how to plan for them.  And
in your current game, AoLS is only necessary because you're not wearing a
cloak or body armor -- which, no matter how you spin it, is a result of
poor planning and impatience, both of which are mistakes.



